{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that","id":984760,"title":"The Rulership & Infrastructure Exalted, if you made Solars just THAT","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-09T23:01:51-07:00","id":984760,"title":"The Rulership & Infrastructure Exalted, if you made Solars just THAT","content":"IIRC, Solars (at least in 2e) have some reliance on infrastructure for some abilities. They work best when they have built a system to feed into them and also have (had?) abilities to build or take over such a system.<br /> <br /> They also could be peerless warriors, thieves or sorcerers or what-have-you. They could dick off into the woods and forget about all that infrastructure bull hickey to kick some major ass by themselves.No need to play Sim City when you're the mastering the FPS.<br /> <br /> So, what happens when you remove these latter bits and expand upon the former? When you make an Exalt, possibly the Solar, into someone who has a hard time working on their own. They can make sweeping changes once they have people working for them. They're really good at getting people to work for them too, but on their own they're just a dude. What would that look like?<br /> <br /> Bonus: Then you take all the bits about being a singularly and lonesomely powerful [whatever] and move them over to the Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T23:53:21-07:00","id":984768,"title":"","content":"I've seen this argument many times before.<br /> <br /> The end result is that you want someone who is capable of doing something by themselves as most games tend to wander in my experience than be settled. Even when settlement does happen, its not until mid-late/late game, so for the majority of the game the Solar is sucking this thumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T00:01:04-07:00","id":984769,"title":"","content":"I would dethrone Solars from their spot as the default, starter splat. Most games are not about establishing yourself in one spot and being a leader of men.<br /> <br /> It would also make it more difficult to portray certain types of heroes. Who is Sherlock Holmes now? Captain America? Because Lunars are still shape-shifters with a primal bent, even if they're the strongest, smartest, most charismatic, and while that fits some heroes, it clashes with others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T00:11:14-07:00","id":984772,"title":"","content":"So I would have to wait for the Lunar book to come out if I want to play my wandering Invincible Sword Uncle ? Ummm no, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T00:44:46-07:00","id":984777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=984772#post984772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I would have to wait for the Lunar book to come out if I want to play my wandering Invincible Sword Uncle ? Ummm no, thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see:<br /> Dragon-Blood - 2017<br /> Exigents - 2018<br /> Abyssals and Liminals - 2019<br /> Lunars - 2020<br /> Sidereals - 2021<br /> <br /> That's just a couple of years.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T01:17:54-07:00","id":984783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=984777#post984777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just a couple of years.</div> </div> </div> </div>This year has not even ended yet and I'm already hungry for more books, if I have to wait 4 more years to play the Uncle then I'll seriously explode.......<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T01:21:42-07:00","id":984785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=984777#post984777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's see:<br /> Dragon-Blood - 2017<br /> Exigents - 2018<br /> Abyssals and Liminals - 2019<br /> Lunars - 2020<br /> Sidereals - 2021<br /> <br /> That's just a couple of years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poor inocent soul.<br /> <br /> Calculate 2020 for DB's, and ??? for everybody else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12278-broken25","name":"Broken25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T01:34:44-07:00","id":984786,"title":"","content":"So essentially, the question is what would happen if you made solars the ultimate bureaucrats? Well, that's a pretty specific skillset. (You'd have charms for what, Socialize, Presence, Integrity, and Bureaucracy?) I mean, it also doesn't make sense in the context of the solars entire purpose for being created; to be the guys who take down the primordials, or the already established authority. It only makes sense in the context of being the solar host, rulers of creation. Considering the solars represent Sol/the Unconquered Sun, AKA the ultimate everything, this is also a strange thematic disconnect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">BEHOLD! GLORIOUS SOLAR MONKEY!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> My avatar was made by <b>Jen!</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12377-raaabr","name":"raaabr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12377_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T04:56:58-07:00","id":984823,"title":"","content":"If I was going to par down the Solar splat, I'd make them the Exalts of Creation. Give all the crazy Wyld charms in craft, Occult, and integrity to Lunars. <br /> <br /> Solars are awesome... As long as they are in creation. In the Wyld, they have to rely on thier Lunar mates for assistance. <br /> <br /> With this idea, I changed chimera from shapeless Lunars to Solars who escaped to the Wyld with thier Lunar mates. They could not handle the Wyld for long periods of time and became monsters. <br /> <br /> There is obvious holes in the idea, but it makes a good though experiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:31:13-07:00","id":985000,"title":"","content":"Not a bad idea for an alternate shardworld. I think you'd have to recharacterise the Unconquered Sun, their patron, as a wise king and grand organizer, ruling through cleverness and wisdom, and not the strongest in personal might, and the muscular, personally magnetic bruiser he is.<br /> <br /> I think I like the canon a bit better where the returning Solars are to a large degree two fisted, personally mighty heroes with a lot of strength, more than, &quot;It's the return of the very clever and charismatic people&quot; who aren't that personally mighty (even though, confession, Eclipse are the best Solars), but that's me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a>, the Solar Chimera idea is a pretty cool idea. (Also if anyone wanted to explore that space in a game (some Solars escaped to the Wyld and were changed), an alternative might be you could also have some of the escaping Solars from the Usurpation become like the Eternal Revolutionary or Eos and Ossia, where they are archetypal, reduced versions of themselves...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:39:23-07:00","id":985039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=984777#post984777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's see:<br /> Dragon-Blood - 2017<br /> Exigents - 2018<br /> Abyssals and Liminals - 2019<br /> Lunars - 2020<br /> Sidereals - 2021<br /> <br /> That's just a couple of years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this is OT, but... are Abyssals and Liminals really slated before Lunars and Sidereals? That's a travesty. I know John loves his Underworld; really, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:46:52-07:00","id":985047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985039#post985039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is OT, but... are Abyssals and Liminals really slated before Lunars and Sidereals? That's a travesty. I know John loves his Underworld; really, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty sure Abyssals and Liminals come after Lunars and Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:20:39-07:00","id":985064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985047#post985047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Abyssals and Liminals come after Lunars and Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I would assume so (though for my part I would have expected Exigentsafter Lunars and Sidereals too and I think that's confirmed to be the other way?), but I also figured Hippokrene might have been paying closer attention than me, so one never knows.<br /> <br /> That's enough derailing from me, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:24:05-07:00","id":985066,"title":"","content":"Exigents will give players a Homebrew toolkit, so that is why it comes after Dragonblooded, but before Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:22:54-07:00","id":985117,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm missing something, but I don't see any benefit of hacking off 75% of the Solars' power set and bolting it onto Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:28:59-07:00","id":985120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985117#post985117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm missing something, but I don't see any benefit of hacking off 75% of the Solars' power set and bolting it onto Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea is separate than the OP's idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:31:26-07:00","id":985150,"title":"","content":"Don't you just get Alchemicals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:58:57-07:00","id":985227,"title":"","content":"Well, for one thing you'd need a Bureaucracy system to actually exist, and a rulership system that doesn't come down to &quot;throw Merits at the problem,&quot; and advise against the characters actually getting directly involved in solving problems on the grounds that if the PCs actually <i>do things</i>, they're neglecting their responsibilities &quot;at home.&quot; The way the section on leadership is written, if a terrible monster is ravaging the countryside and your Twilight Caste Solar casts Conjuring the Azure Chariot to carry the circle to the right area, his Zenith reassures the locals and leads them away from the combat zone, her Dawn and her friend's Night kill the monster in short order, that other player's Eclipse takes a survey of the damage and available resources and sets up an ad hoc relief and reconstruction organization, and the whole circle's back home in time for tea, you're doing it wrong. The correct method is to use your Followers Merit to have people investigate the monster sightings, then your Command Merit to dispatch the army, then your Resources Merit and Followers Merit to have supplies and workers sent to assist in the rebuilding, and your Cult Merit to have priests assure the populace that you are always doing the very best ting for the kingdom. Yes, I do recognize that the circle can't always attend directly to a problem, and often shouldn't. But the Leadership section as written actively discourages any direct involvement, and the devs have directly stated that they don't want any system that allows Solars to throw lots of dice at their problems, which kind of works against the theme of returned and glorious god-kings. Why bother with kingship when you're actively encouraged to not do anything any ordinary ruler couldn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T00:36:46-07:00","id":985306,"title":"","content":"&quot;I use my Athletics charms to leap across the raging river! ... just as soon as my minions build a bridge over it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T00:58:05-07:00","id":985310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985039#post985039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is OT, but... are Abyssals and Liminals really slated before Lunars and Sidereals? That's a travesty. I know John loves his Underworld; really, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just teasing Jen.<br /> <br /> We know that it will be Dragon-Blooded and Exigents next. Dev comments suggest that Infernals and Alchemicals will be later than the other major splats.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I don't think we have any information, explicit or inferred, as to what splat will be dropping when. Sorry to disappoint!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T03:29:28-07:00","id":985340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985227#post985227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for one thing you'd need a Bureaucracy system to actually exist\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>It may not be as robust as you want, but by no means does that make it somehow not a system.<br /> <br /> \u2026huh. Deja vu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-11-2016, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T08:34:24-07:00","id":985437,"title":"","content":"&quot;[N]ot as robust as [I] might like&quot; consists of &quot;roll some dice, make stuff up.&quot; And the &quot;roll some dice&quot; part is only implied. Seriously. Would you consider the combat system acceptable if it was just &quot;&quot;make stuff up?&quot; Or the social system? Of course not. You'd want at least some suggestions or rough guidelines to difficulties, penalties and bonuses, wouldn't you? These are not available for Bureaucracy. There are some vague suggestions that can be gleaned by examination of the Bureaucracy Charms, but that's it. Bureaucracy in the current edition has exactly no mechanical support. &quot;This Charm speeds the progress of any bureaucratic activity&quot; means nothing if the time required is already nothing but fiat. There's not even a list of actions Bureaucracy might be used to undertake. Sail is obvious: you use Sail for navigation and ship handling. Ride is obvious: you use Ride to handle and ride various mounts. You use Bureaucracy to... um... bargain with merchants and find great deals! Meaning what, with the Resources system being so vague and the scale so crude? You use it to organize the labour involved in major projects! Except that falls under Craft. You use it keep an army fed and supplied! OK, that one's valid. But what's the difficulty? What penalties and bonuses might apply? How do the various Charms help with that? Or in interfering with your opponents' logistics train? No idea. Not even a suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:07:32-07:00","id":985454,"title":"","content":"It seems like there's a history here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T10:11:47-07:00","id":985486,"title":"","content":"Alucard reacts very poorly to any suggestion that the current mechanics are in any way inadequate. I view the current mechanics from point of view of systems analysis, which I have formally studied. And from that point of view, there are several areas in which the current mechanics are inadequate (Resources), non-existent (Bureaucracy), or unfitting (Craft). Naturally enough, this leads to intense disagreements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T10:44:58-07:00","id":985505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985227#post985227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> rulership system that doesn't come down to &quot;throw Merits at the problem,&quot; and advise against the characters actually getting directly involved in solving problems on the grounds that if the PCs actually <i>do things</i>, they're neglecting their responsibilities &quot;at home.&quot; The way the section on leadership is written, if a terrible monster is ravaging the countryside and your Twilight Caste Solar casts Conjuring the Azure Chariot to carry the circle to the right area, his Zenith reassures the locals and leads them away from the combat zone, her Dawn and her friend's Night kill the monster in short order, that other player's Eclipse takes a survey of the damage and available resources and sets up an ad hoc relief and reconstruction organization, and the whole circle's back home in time for tea, you're doing it wrong. The correct method is to use your Followers Merit to have people investigate the monster sightings, then your Command Merit to dispatch the army, then your Resources Merit and Followers Merit to have supplies and workers sent to assist in the rebuilding, and your Cult Merit to have priests assure the populace that you are always doing the very best ting for the kingdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just re-read the leadership section...and I missed all this. Like, I don't see where it says you shouldn't get involved. I see clearly the &quot;here's how to use merits to help&quot; part, but not the &quot;so therefore never go it alone&quot; part. Granted, it also reads to me like a Storyteller advice system more than a cruch system, but that's a different problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985227#post985227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, I do recognize that the circle can't always attend directly to a problem, and often shouldn't. But the Leadership section as written actively discourages any direct involvement, and the devs have directly stated that they don't want any system that allows Solars to throw lots of dice at their problems, which kind of works against the theme of returned and glorious god-kings. Why bother with kingship when you're actively encouraged to not do anything any ordinary ruler couldn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the problem was making rulership more than &quot;And then I roll to wage war&quot; or &quot;And then I roll to reform the church&quot;, and making those indepth hard work things you do, applying your abillities and merits to the right places to secure things (where your glory shines, but not as a single action, but the abillity to do multiple nigh-impossible actions). But this half also relies on the &quot;rule don't want you to do things yourself&quot; part...and I don't see that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T10:54:49-07:00","id":985512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985486#post985486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alucard reacts very poorly to any suggestion that the current mechanics are in any way inadequate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inaccurate. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985486#post985486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I view the current mechanics from point of view of systems analysis, which I have formally studied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Congratulations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985486#post985486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And from that point of view, there are several areas in which the current mechanics are inadequate (Resources)\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Inadequate <i>to you</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985486#post985486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026non-existent (Bureaucracy)\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect, <i>again</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985486#post985486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026or unfitting (Craft).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because you, or even a number of people, don't <i>like</i> something, doesn't mean it's <i>bad</i>. People being allergic to shellfish doesn't make popcorn shrimp <i>bad</i>, it just means that it's a thing that's not for everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985486#post985486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naturally enough, this leads to intense disagreements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure <i>that's</i> what leads to the disagreements?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Not as robust as I might like&quot; consists of &quot;roll some dice, make stuff up.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Roll some dice, make stuff up&quot; is literally the core mechanic of the entire game. I don't know why you'd expect a system to not use that in places.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the &quot;roll some dice&quot; part is only implied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly. It's right there at the beginning of the Systems chapter. If a situation calls for it, roll some dice, make stuff up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously. Would you consider the combat system acceptable if it was just &quot;&quot;make stuff up?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>For some Exalted groups? Yes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the social system?</div> </div> </div> </div>For some Exalted groups? Yes.<br /> <br /> More importantly, I don't expect many groups to be getting as deeply into bureaucracy as groups generally get into combat or socializing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hereby revoke any permission I might have ever given you to speak for me, here, because you're dead wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd want at least some suggestions or rough guidelines to difficulties, penalties and bonuses, wouldn't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right there, beginning of the systems chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are not available for Bureaucracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correction: these are not <i>separate</i> for Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some vague suggestions that can be gleaned by examination of the Bureaucracy Charms, but that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right there by the beginning of the system chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bureaucracy in the current edition has exactly no mechanical support.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might view it as a bad thing, but the fact of the matter is that giving the Storyteller so much freedom in this new edition <i>requires</i> that the Storyteller be willing to run with that freedom, which includes making things up, often on the fly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;This Charm speeds the progress of any bureaucratic activity&quot; means nothing if the time required is already nothing but fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this line of thinking even make sense to you? If I say four hours, and it cuts it in half, <i>that means two hours</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not even a list of actions Bureaucracy might be used to undertake.</div> </div> </div> </div>And? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sail is obvious: you use Sail for navigation and ship handling. Ride is obvious: you use Ride to handle and ride various mounts. You use Bureaucracy to... um... bargain with merchants and find great deals!</div> </div> </div> </div>Among other things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meaning what, with the Resources system being so vague and the scale so crude?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because you don't see meaning doesn't mean something is meaningless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You use it to organize the labour involved in major projects! Except that falls under Craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of it, surely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You use it keep an army fed and supplied! OK, that one's valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>How convenient of you to defeat your own argument for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what's the difficulty? What penalties and bonuses might apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>System chapter, right by the beginning. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the various Charms help with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps to read the Charms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or in interfering with your opponents' logistics train? No idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps to read the Charms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985437#post985437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even a suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>System chapter, right- ah, forget it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-11-2016, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:17:46-07:00","id":985531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985306#post985306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I use my Athletics charms to leap across the raging river! ... just as soon as my minions build a bridge over it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this <i>could</i> work if the most basic Solar charms in each ability gave them Pikmin-style miniature servants everywhere they go for that ability's tasks.<br /> <br /> So a Melee Solar has a swarm of tiny foot-tall soldiers who attack or block with them whenever they attack or block. An Athletics Solar has a swarm of little people who lift them over barriers, etc. It's like playing Tron Bonne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:44:48-07:00","id":985556,"title":"","content":"The combat system begins on page 189, and ends on page 213. Remove that entire section. Also remove all references outside of that section to health levels, other than references in the Charm section, and remove pages 580 to 601, which includes the statistics for all the various weapons and armours. What remains is exactly the amount of support the system gives to Bureaucracy. Tell me, Alucard, do you consider that an adequate amount of support? I happen to be of the opinion that a game should provide rules for the actions it claims to support. Would you favour removing from chess the rules on pawn movement? It's exactly equivalent: A portion of the game which is implied to be of great importance (after all, half your starting pieces are pawns) with no mechanical support (how do you use them? No clue, make something up). This would be considered completely unacceptable in chess, why is it acceptable in Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:54:12-07:00","id":985564,"title":"","content":"Hey while we are throwing our credentialed weight around, I've professionally consulted on game balance and design for 10 years; and I think the lack of a Bureaucracy system is absolutely the best way they could have gone about it. Wait, that doesn't matter at all, does it?<br /> <br /> In my opinion, what they didn't do was provide examples and help frame things such that people who have no background in how bureaucracy actually works so they could use it effectively beyond a lot of handwaving.<br /> <br /> Also, fun fact, did you know that games with formalized rules and competitive structures make bad comparisons to games with open-ended structures and no hard walls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":".  Clarified 2nd sentence because I can't even sentence structure goodly 10-11-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:58:59-07:00","id":985571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985564#post985564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey while we are throwing our credentialed weight around, I've professionally consulted on game balance and design for 10 years; and I think the lack of a Bureaucracy system is absolutely the best way they could have gone about it. Wait, that doesn't matter at all, does it?<br /> <br /> In my opinion, what they didn't do was provide examples and help frame things such that people who have no background in how bureaucracy actually works to use it effectively beyond a lot of handwaving.<br /> <br /> Also, fun fact, did you know that games with formalized rules and competitive structures make bad comparisons to games with open-ended structures and no hard walls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why the never imported the CRM system in I'll never know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:06:36-07:00","id":985582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985505#post985505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Just re-read the leadership section...and I missed all this. Like, I don't see where it says you shouldn't get involved. I see clearly the &quot;here's how to use merits to help&quot; part, but not the &quot;so therefore never go it alone&quot; part. Granted, it also reads to me like a Storyteller advice system more than a cruch system, but that's a different problem.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I thought the problem was making rulership more than &quot;And then I roll to wage war&quot; or &quot;And then I roll to reform the church&quot;, and making those indepth hard work things you do, applying your abillities and merits to the right places to secure things (where your glory shines, but not as a single action, but the abillity to do multiple nigh-impossible actions). But this half also relies on the &quot;rule don't want you to do things yourself&quot; part...and I don't see that.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I also just re-read it. Almost all of the section is about directing others, using Merits, and working through others. The first paragraph after the introduction explicitly states &quot;[L]eaders concave ambitions and delegate the work necessary to realize them.&quot; The rest of the section assumes that the work is in fact delegated, quite clearly. The last two sentences under &quot;Responding to Failure Conditions&quot; read &quot;</span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Finally, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the character might attempt to address failure conditions directly with her own Abilities and Charms, or through </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">mighty sorcery. This is often an attractive option, given the </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">prowess of the Exalted, but a leader off personally resolv</span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">ing problems may be neglecting other matters close to home.&quot; A page and a half written on the clear assumption of the PCs not doing things directly and which ends with advising against the PCs actually doing things directly strongly suggests that the authors do not favour the PCs doing things directly once they become leaders.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because you, or even a number of people, don't <i>l</i> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>ike</i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> something, doesn't mean it's </span></span><i>bad</i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">. People being allergic to shellfish doesn't make popcorn shrimp </span></span><i>bad</i><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">, it just means that it's a thing that's not for everyone.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">To use a less faulty analogy, if a significant percentage of the players first edition AD&amp;D, find the grappling rules cumbersome and un-fun, this can be legitimately viewed as an indication that the rule- in question are ill-conceived and in need of revision, removal, or replacement.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 10-11-2016, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:10:59-07:00","id":985587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985564#post985564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey while we are throwing our credentialed weight around, I've professionally consulted on game balance and design for 10 years; and I think the lack of a Bureaucracy system is absolutely the best way they could have gone about it. Wait, that doesn't matter at all, does it?<br /> <br /> In my opinion, what they didn't do was provide examples and help frame things such that people who have no background in how bureaucracy actually works to use it effectively beyond a lot of handwaving.<br /> <br /> Also, fun fact, did you know that games with formalized rules and competitive structures make bad comparisons to games with open-ended structures and no hard walls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this is useful commentary. The absence of a dedicated Bureaucracy system is not a fatal blow to the ability's usefulness, but the complete lack of any form of examples, guidance, or even suggestions on how to use the ability in question is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 10-12-2016, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T23:50:00-07:00","id":985976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985571#post985571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why the never imported the CRM system in I'll never know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core book was already too damn big and taking too much time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T00:34:09-07:00","id":985986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/984760-the-rulership-infrastructure-exalted-if-you-made-solars-just-that?p=985571#post985571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the never imported the CRM system in I'll never know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs already addressed this - the CRM system trivializes people acting like people in the setting, turning them into rational widgets that a Solar can control at any level of size or complexity. It doesn't work the way they'd like running an organization to work in Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCou